"helpText" = "## How to use\n1. Select several lines of text and copy them (⌘C).\n2. Click where you want to paste and press **⌃⌥V**. The first line is pasted.\n3. Move to the next place (Tab, click, etc.) and press **⌃⌥V** again to paste the second line. Repeat until the last line.\n- About a second after each paste, the remaining lines are put back on the clipboard (same as the Keyboard Maestro macro). After the last line, the clipboard is emptied.\n- If you copy other text in between, the next ⌃⌥V starts from its first line.\n- The main window lists the lines to paste next and how many are left.\n- The result stays in \"Last result\" in the main window and at the top of the menu bar menu. Failures are shown near the top of the screen.\n\n## Line cleanup\nWhen copied text is loaded, it is cleaned up in this order (Settings > Paste):\n1. Remove leading spaces, tabs and ideographic spaces\n2. Remove a leading \"・\", \"* \", \"- \", \"1. \" (number + period) or \"①–㊿\"\n- Blank lines (including whitespace-only lines) are always skipped. LF, CRLF and CR line breaks are all supported.\n\n## Click any line (any order)\nSame as the Keyboard Maestro macro \"02)非連続ペースト\".\n1. Copy several lines and place the cursor in the target app.\n2. In the PasteInARow window, click the line you want. The app you used last comes back to the front and the line is pasted there; it is removed from the list.\n3. Move to the next place and click another line in any order.\n- ⌥-click pastes the line followed by a line break.\n- Paste All pastes the remaining lines at once; Clear removes them and empties the clipboard (Start Over brings them back).\n- ⌃⌥V and clicks share the same list.\n\n## Start over\n- \"Start Over from the First Line\" (main window, File menu, menu bar) puts the whole copied text back on the clipboard; the next ⌃⌥V starts from the first line.\n- Not available after another copy. The text is kept in memory only and discarded on quit.\n\n## Settings\n- Launch & Background: launch at login (off by default), hide main window at startup, keep running, menu bar icon, Accessibility status, restart and quit buttons.\n- Hotkey: enable/disable ⌃⌥V, pause (until relaunch), change (Esc cancels recording), reset.\n- Paste: line cleanup, notification after each paste (off by default).\n- Excluded Apps: apps where ⌃⌥V is not used, identified by Bundle ID. Defaults: Illustrator, Path Finder, Keynote.\n- About: version and links.\n- Open Settings with ⌘, and close it with ⌘W.\n\n## Hotkey\n- **⌃⌥V**: paste the next line (not registered while an excluded app is in front, so that app gets the key; the front app is checked again right after the press).\n- The Keyboard Maestro macro also uses ⌃⌥V. If both are enabled, both run; disable one of them.\n\n## Permission\n- **Accessibility** is needed to send Paste (⌘V) to the front app. Turn on PasteInARow in System Settings > Privacy & Security > Accessibility. Settings > Launch & Background has a button that opens it.\n- Without it, ⌃⌥V shows the reason and does not change the clipboard.\n\n## Running and quitting\n- PasteInARow stays in the menu bar; ⌃⌥V works with the window closed.\n- Reopen the main window from the menu bar icon, the Dock, Finder or ⌘0.\n- Quit with \"Quit PasteInARow\" in the menu bar menu, or ⌘Q while the app is in front.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n- **Nothing happens**: check Accessibility, that the hotkey is enabled and not paused, and that the front app is not excluded.\n- **Lines are skipped or pasted twice**: the Keyboard Maestro macro is also enabled. Disable one of them.\n- **The hotkey cannot be registered**: another app uses the same key. Choose another one in Settings > Hotkey.\n\n## Privacy\n- Everything runs on this Mac; nothing is sent out (except update checks).\n- Clipboard text is kept in memory only while pasting, never written to files or logs.";
